itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025    WHO of the gods was HE?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?Who kindled rage between the chiefs?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?Who, but the son of Latona and high-thundering Jove?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?HE\uc1 \u8212 ?rouzed to wrath against the king,\uc1 \u8212 ?threw death and disease, among the host.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?The people perished before him.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?The son of Atreus had dishonoured his priest.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?White-haired, the aged Chryses came\uc1 \u8212 ?to the swift ships of the Argive powers.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?He came to redeem his daughter.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?The high-prized ransom is borne before.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?In his hands is the wreath of the god,\uc1 \u8212 ?the golden scepter of far-shooting Ph\uc1 \u339 ?bus.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?The aged suppliant, Greece addressed,\uc1 \u8212 ?but most addressed the sons of Atreus:\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?The two leaders of the nations in war! }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi240 \li0 \ri0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \uc1 \u8220 ?SONS of Atreus!\uc1 \u8221 ? he said: \uc1 \u8220 ?Other warriors of Achaia hear!\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?May the gods crown all your desires!\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?May the deathless dwellers of heaven give ear,\uc1 \u8212 ?and grant to YOU, the city of Priam: With a safe return to your native land.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?But release my much-loved daughter.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?Receive her ransom from these hands.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?Revere the son of thundering Jove: Apollo, who shoots from afar!\uc1 \u8221 ? }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi240 \li0 \ri0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?APPLAUDING Greece arose around.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?The holy man they all revered.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?They wished to take the splendid prize.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?But the soul of Agamemnon refused.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?HIM he dismissed with contempt,\uc1 \u8212 ?and thus added threats to his rage:\uc1 \u8212 ?\uc1 \u8220 ?Take heed, I say, old man!\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?Lest that scepter, that wreath of thy god,\uc1 \u8212 ?should not in ought avail.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?HER I will never release,\uc1 \u8212 ?till age her lovely form invades,\uc1 \u8212 ?within our lofty halls in Argos,\uc1 \u8212 ?far from her native land: While she runs o\uc1 \u8217 ?er the web\uc1 \u8212 ?and ascends the bed of her lord.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?Hence!\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?Provoke me not\uc1 \u8212 ?that safe thou may\uc1 \u8217 ?st still retire.\uc1 \u8221 ?}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?HE, frowning, spoke:\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?The old man feared,\uc1 \u8212 ?and shrunk from his high commands.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?Sad, silent, slow, he took his way,\uc1 \u8212 ?along the wide-resounding main.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?Apart and distant from the host,\uc1 \u8212 ?he poured his mournful soul in prayer:\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?He poured it forth to bowyer Ph\uc1 \u339 ?bus,\uc1 \u8212 ?whom the long-haired Latona bore. }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u8220 ?HEAR, bearer of the splendid bow!\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?Guardian of Chrysa, of Cilla, the divine!\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?Thou that o\uc1 \u8217 ?er Tenedos reign\uc1 \u8217 ?st with fame!\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?O Smintheus, hear my prayer!\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?If ever with wreaths I adorned,\uc1 \u8212 ?O Ph\uc1 \u339 ?bus! Thy beauteous fane:\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?If ever thine altars smoked with offerings\uc1 \u8212 ?from the flocks and herds of Chryses:\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?If ME thou regardest in ought\uc1 \u8212 ?O Ph\uc1 \u339 ?bus,\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?hear my prayer!\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?Punish Greece for these tears of mine.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?Send thy deadly arrow abroad.\uc1 \u8221 ? }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?HE praying spoke.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?Apollo heard.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?He descended, from heaven, enraged in soul.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?On his shoulders his bow is hung: His quiver filled with deadly shafts:\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?Which harshly rattled, as he strode in his wrath.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?Like Night he is borne along:\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?Then darkly-sitting, apart from the host,\uc1 \u8212 ?he sends an arrow abroad.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?The bright bow emits a dreadful sound,\uc1 \u8212 ?as the shaft flies, unseen, from the string.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?Mules, first, the angry god invades:\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?Then fleetly-bounding dogs are slain:\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?Soon, on the heroes themselves,\uc1 \u8212 ?the death-devoting arrow falls.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?The frequent piles are flaming to heaven. }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 REVIEW COMMENT}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 Macpherson is particularly impressed with the \uc1 \u8220 ?simplicity\uc1 \u8221 ? of Homer and, in his introduction, observes that contemporary taste in poetry does not allow poetical translators to deliver that aspect of the original: \uc1 \u8220 ?The best translators have not . . . occupied the whole ground.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?The simplicity, the gravity, the characteristical diction, and perhaps, a great part of the dignity of Homer, are left untouched.\uc1 \u160 ?They have rendered the father of poetry, in a great measure, their own:\uc1 \u160 ?And, in stripping him of his ancient weeds, they have made him too much of a modern beau.\uc1 \u8221 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?By choosing prose, Macpherson hopes he has been faithful to the simplicity of expression and smoothness of language of the original and assures us that he has \uc1 \u8220 ?translated the Greek VERBATIM.\uc1 \u8221 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 The result is an English style which must be among the simplest and most straightforward ever offered in a translation of Homer, with no attempt to involve traditional \uc1 \u8220 ?poetical\uc1 \u8221 ? effects from the past or the present.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?Typically, Macpherson keeps the clauses so short (with sentences often broken up by punctuation into even shorter units) that the effect is one of continuously stopping and starting, a technique which, for all its extreme clarity and directness, prevents the Homeric lines from accumulating much momentum as a long sentence unwinds (a common feature of the Homeric simile and some of the battle descriptions) and creates a certain monotony in the sentence structure.\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?But the prose is for the most part accurate, energetic, and free from artifice. }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 To access the Volume I of the Macpherson translation, click on the following